    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d502">

                <pb facs="0715" n="609" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg609"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Minister
                    Dawson.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-07-11"><hi rendition="#italic">July 11,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 120.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    No. 261, of the 16th ultimo, reporting on the Dominican-Haitian boundary
                    controversy.</p>
                <p>The intelligence and industry shown by you in the preparation of your report are
                    highly commended.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Bacon.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
